WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.481
Reviews only matter if you
can prove they happened,

2
00:00:03.481 --> 00:00:07.238
so the last piece reads every
decision back, for the ISSO.

3
00:00:07.238 --> 00:00:11.546
Each decision becomes a row: who
was reviewed, what was decided,

4
00:00:11.546 --> 00:00:14.925
by whom, when, and whether
it was actually applied.

5
00:00:14.925 --> 00:00:19.942
Then come the checks an assessor cares
about: a series that's missing or overdue,

6
00:00:19.942 --> 00:00:24.418
a denial that didn't take effect,
silence deciding for a sensitive role,

7
00:00:24.418 --> 00:00:28.354
approvals with no reason, someone
reviewing their own access,

8
00:00:28.354 --> 00:00:32.213
a burst of identical clicks,
and an emergency account denied.

9
00:00:32.213 --> 00:00:35.660
The rows name people, so
treat the folder as evidence.
